 "verdict": {
  "slot_convention": "slot 3*t+k holds the edge between triangle positions k+2 and k (i.e. vertex k-1 -> vertex k; the edge opposite vertex k+1). Equivalently, edge j = Vj -> V(j+1) is stored in slot (j+1)%3. 32,700 of 32,700 interior slots in 19 meshes; 0 for k->k+1 or k+1->k+2.",
  "edge_test_1995fa0": "consistent: for edge j the slot (j+1)%3 neighbour shares Vj and V(j+1) in 32,700/32,700 cases, and 'the vertex after VA in the neighbour' is the neighbour's opposite (non-shared) vertex in 32,700/32,700. Reading slot j instead would reach a triangle across a different edge in 32,700/32,700. The (j+1)%3 offset is the storage convention, not a quirk.",
  "fan_walk_1996280": "consistent: slot pos(v) is the edge (previous vertex, v), so each step crosses an edge incident to v into a triangle that contains v (32,700/32,700 first steps). On the 16 closed meshes every walk returns to the start, visits every incident triangle and tests every ring vertex. On the 3 open meshes 12 walks per mesh (36) stop at 0xffff; 24 of them miss incident triangles and 36 miss ring vertices (the documented one-way walk)."
 },
